Third-party components bundled in release artifacts

Every release archive and npm package also contains the components below. They
are not covered by the Apache License, Version 2.0; each remains under its own
license. The pinned versions, digests and download locations are recorded in
the manifests under third_party/.

* ripgrep 15.2.0 (https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep), MIT OR Unlicense.
  Shipped as the codex-path search backend; see third_party/ripgrep/sources.json.

* bubblewrap 0.13.0 (https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap),
  LGPL-2.0-or-later. Shipped as the Linux sandbox launcher; see
  third_party/bwrap/sources.json. The corresponding source is the unmodified
  upstream release tarball
  (https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap/releases/download/v0.13.0/bubblewrap-0.13.0.tar.xz),
  which is built unmodified by third_party/bwrap/prepare_bwrap.py and can be
  obtained from that URL or requested from the distributor for at least three
  years after the last distribution of the binary.

* Opus 1.5.2 (https://opus-codec.org), BSD-3-Clause. Linked into the packaged
  voice runtime; see third_party/voice/sources.json.

